  "body": "Scaling laws are one of the most critical empirical findings in deep learning. The observation is simple in form: the training loss L decreases predictably as we scale up model size N, dataset size D, and compute C, following a power-law curve, which appears as a straight line on a log-log plot. We can view scaling laws as a framework for describing the relationship between compute, loss, model size and data; at its core, it is about how to allocate precious compute optimally between N and D.",
